# JOURNEY · fish with an Angler Rig: a rail casts once, the player's one Bait goes down, a fish comes up.
# Rod's coil makes it a rail on go, which is also its rig's cast: it rises once, from the cold first stage.
# A rig never fishes quickly (economy epic): its line stays down RIG_WAIT_MIN_SECS to RIG_WAIT_MAX_SECS
# (30 to 60 game seconds) and always lands a fish, so the play slows the world to one second a tick and
# waits 100 ticks. caught is high for one stage only, so Bell, a bare botfish that hears caught and its
# own output, latches it: Bell's dot lights in /circuit once the catch is in, and the tank holds three.
# Bought: an Inverter Coil and an Angler Rig at the bench and one Bait at the counter; the Computer and
# both botfish are found, never sold, so the scenes hand them over.
# Rod's panel walks by count: listens, drives, threshold, cast, caught.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/grow-a-matrixtank.play
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Inverter Coil" Fabric
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Angler Rig" Hands
include scenes/take-a-fish.play botfish rod
include scenes/take-a-fish.play botfish bell

run /shop
key enter
select Bait
key enter
expect < 1 >
snap one bait on the counter
key enter
key esc
key esc
absent Price/unit

run /consume inverter coil
key enter
run /consume angler rig
expect Angler Rig to the botfishes
snap the install picker offers the Angler Rig to Rod
key enter
absent to the botfishes

run /program "Bell"
type caught, held
key down
type held
snap Bell hears caught and holds itself up
key enter
absent listens

run /fps 1
run /program "Rod"
key down
type go
key down 2
expect threshold
type go
key down
type caught
snap Rod is a rail on go, which casts its rig once
key enter
absent listens

expect 2/50
tick 100
expect 3/50
snap a fish came up and joined the tank
run /circuit
expect ●  Bell
snap Bell caught the pulse the rig raised when something came up
key esc
absent Circuit#
